{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773086815,"nonce":"4wj63YQA9KesKBNIAG9nZm78BKk=","title":"graph API: session_issues unbounded scan + getIssueDetail spawnSync blocking","message":"Two performance issues in the graph endpoint (GET /api/graph):\n\n1. session_issues full-table scan (graph.ts ~line 282): `SELECT session_id, issue_id, repo_id FROM session_issues` has no time/limit filter. The table grows unboundedly; on an active instance this becomes tens of thousands of rows fetched on every SSE-triggered graph refresh.\nFix: filter WHERE session_id IN (\u003calready-fetched session IDs\u003e) or join against the sessions query.\n\n2. getIssueDetail() spawnSync in HTTP handler (graph.ts umbrella_child section): Called once per umbrella issue to get description text. This is spawnSync with 15s timeout and 3 retries — blocks the Node event loop per call.\nFix: cache issue descriptions in IssueScanner during the list scan (run async parallel fetches at scan time), or build umbrella_child edges at scan time rather than per-request.\n\nBoth are performance issues; the graph view is functional but will degrade under load or with many umbrella issues. The sync spawnSync issue is higher priority.\n\nBug: fe566dc","files":null}]}